On 1 jul, 17:57, rg <roger.g.gr...@gmail.com> wrote:
> I have an ES40 with 4 CPU and 4 GB memory and several SCSI drives.
> When I hit the power on button, the fans begin to spin up and about 2
> seconds later it power down and the OCP says system down. =A0Any ideas
> where to start?

Something similar happened with a dual cpu alpha server 1200. The cpu
has a small
fan mounted on top of it. One of the fans didn't spin up and the
system powers down before actual damage is done.

If you're without manuals and no clear idea where the problem is
located, try pulling all processors but one and all
memory boards but one. If the system boots then you can add components
until you hit the faulty one(s).
If it doesn't then remove the remaing cpu and memory and restart. If
it still shuts down then remove all pci boards.
The general idea is to find a hardware configuration that doen't shut
down and remains stable. Once you've got that you
can add components one by one and figure out which one(s) cause the
unit to fail.
Of course, as Kari already pointed out, a manual is greatly simplifies
this.
Good luck,
Hans


