Robert Jarratt wrote:
> I have a jammed TK50 cartridge in a TZ87. Before I start dismantling too 
> much I wanted to check one thing. Ordinarily, would I expect to be able 
> to freely turn the take-up spool inside the TZ87 and expect the TK50 
> cartridge to let tape out?

Yes, assuming that nothing is jammed.

What I think happened in your case is what happened to me:
The tape has become stuck to the read/write head!   I had to
disassemble the drive and gently pull the tape off the head.

Back in the 1980s, tape manufacturers used a formulation that,
after time, became sticky.   I am told (but have not tried it
myself), that gently heating (120 degrees F ??) the tape in
a dry atmosphere (a food dehydrator?  an incubator?) will
restore the tape for a short time.   I have had this happen
with TK50, TK70, and 9-track tapes.

There have been several articles written about this problem, but
I can't find them right now (I *really* have to de-clutter this place!).

Alan


