The point is really baking the moisture out of the binder, not
just warming.  It may take some time.  Preservation folks figure
once the tape is properly baked, you get _ONE_ chance at reading it.
The syndrome is called "sticky shed", which might help the googling.
Most of the preservation work on this problem has been done in the
internet era, so a fair proportion of the papers and such are likely
to be available online.

